"      glucose course does."
msgstr ""
"<b>The loop figures need CamAPS FX (Auto Mode).</b>\n"
"      They are read from modulated basal. Other AID systems\n"
"      (e.g. Control-IQ, Omnipod&nbsp;5, AndroidAPS) give their corrections as\n"
"      boluses, so those figures do not apply there — the assessment from the\n"
"      glucose course does."

#: templates/upload.html.j2:176
msgid ""
"<b>Everything stays on this device.</b>\n"
"      No account, no sign-in, nothing sent to a server. The export is deleted as\n"
"      soon as the report has been built from it, and the report itself when the app\n"
"      is closed — at the latest a quarter of an hour later."
msgstr ""
"<b>Everything stays on this device.</b>\n"
"      No account, no sign-in, nothing sent to a server. The export is deleted as\n"
"      soon as the report has been built from it, and the report itself when the app\n"
"      is closed — at the latest a quarter of an hour later."

#: templates/upload.html.j2:180
msgid ""
"<b>Homelab / private.</b>\n"
"      While the analysis runs, the upload and the finished report sit in a private\n"
"      folder in the system temp area. The export itself is deleted as soon\n"
"      as the report exists; the report follows after 15 minutes at the latest.\n"
"      Until then it stays open so you can still save it. No public hosting, no "
"archive."
msgstr ""
"<b>Homelab / private.</b>\n"
"      While the analysis runs, the upload and the finished report sit in a private\n"
"      folder in the system temp area. The export itself is deleted as soon\n"
"      as the report exists; the report follows after 15 minutes at the latest.\n"
"      Until then it stays open so you can still save it. No public hosting, no "
"archive."

